  Geometry behind the theorem for general q (d = 2):
    fixed point of the odd branch      x_o = -1/(q-2)   (cell (1,1), D = 2 - q)
    point where the two branches agree a   = -1/(q-1)
    the functional delta_a - delta_{x_o} is a left eigenvector of K^- with eigenvalue
    -1/2  iff  e(x_o) = a  iff  2(q-2) = q-1  iff  q = 3.
    q = 3: x_o = -1, e(x_o) = -1/2, a = -1/2, e(x_o) == a: True
    q = 5: x_o = -1/3, e(x_o) = -1/6, a = -1/4, e(x_o) == a: False
    q = 7: x_o = -1/5, e(x_o) = -1/10, a = -1/6, e(x_o) == a: False
    q = 9: x_o = -1/7, e(x_o) = -1/14, a = -1/8, e(x_o) == a: False

